<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What are conveyor guide rails?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Conveyor guide rails, also called conveyor rails, side rails, or side guides, are side-mounted rails that keep products centered on the conveyor belt or <a href="/conveyor-types/roller-conveyors/">roller surface</a>, prevent products from falling off edges, create lanes for multi-row product flow, and orient products for downstream operations. Guide rails are typically made from UHMW polyethylene, stainless steel, or aluminum with UHMW contact strips. Adjustable guide rails allow quick changeover between product sizes.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What is the best material for conveyor guide rails?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
